# Intent: A stop word that works while the robot is speaking (owner request 2026-10-21: he said "stop" mid-sentence and it kept talking). A small MultiNet command list (mn5q8_en: stop, stackchan stop, be quiet, quiet, that's enough, never mind, cancel) runs on the AFE's echo-cancelled audio beside the WakeNet wake word, armed only while the device is in the Speaking state; a hit above 0.85 aborts the reply, which sends the host an abort so it ends the turn silently. Every hit and near-miss is reported to the host as a stop_word device event with the fixed command name and score (never audio or words). Safety: the model is created at start-up and dropped for good if it costs more than 6 KB of internal RAM, and arming is refused below 16 KB free internal RAM; both are logged and reported. The AFE processing task stack stays in PSRAM and grows to 12 KB so the deeper detect() call costs no internal RAM. The asset build packs the multinet model beside the wakenet model, and the engine treats a multinet model as the stop word (not a custom wake word) unless CONFIG_USE_CUSTOM_WAKE_WORD is set.
# Placement: unit (the audio path runs on the robot)
# Upstream: main/audio/engines/afe_audio_engine.{h,cc}, main/audio/audio_service.{h,cc}, main/application.cc and scripts/build_default_assets.py of the xiaozhi-esp32 tree (MIT)
